is: The frame, the field read and the send, self-call and super-call forms are as stated (BMCPU/CPU/cpu.hpp:35-46; instructions.hpp:191-220, 1148-1243). The last sentence holds only as: CALLD and FDC are the only forms that move refThis to another object while keeping self (instructions.hpp:1250-1285, 1317-1392). The super call also keeps self and changes refThis, in its interface half only: Super() returns REF( base interface, refThis.Object()) at instructions.hpp:100-103, and CallSuperReg and CallSuperConstant pass CPU.Self() unchanged at 1169-1182 and 1230-1243.
why: The node's own third clause says a super call moves refThis, so 'only CALLD and FDC change refThis while keeping self' contradicts it as written.
