is: The grammar sentence holds only as: no property spells delegate or shared inheritance, and the super-class loop reads neither (Java/jbml/Components/Class.java:495-521). A super-class clause does carry a property list: SuperClass ::= ClassDecl( 3 ) and ClassDecl( context ) ::= FullClassName( id ) Properties( context ) (Java/jbml/JBML.BMF:42, 44, 157), and the compiler reads one property there, moving a super class marked 'class' to the common object's parents (Class.java:177-184). The rest of the node is as stated.
why: The report's line 219 says the rule 'carries no property list'; it quotes JBML.BMF line 44 without line 42. Context 3 is named SUPER_CLASS (Properties/Common.java:11). 'delegate' is a member property (JBML.BMF:149) and 'shared' an array property (JBML.BMF:137).
limit: Confirmed in the archive: the hidden delegate field (ObjectModel/BMLInstanceDefinition.java:99-110), the constructor parameter (Class.java:524-532), the fdc and fcx stub (Class.java:311-337; ASM/Method.java:90-99) and the common-object field (Class.java:477-489).
