ack: node
is: The 2026 sentence is true word for word and does not bear on bounds: template-kind-constraints names which kinds of definition a template may wrap. What shows that 2026 enforces no bound is the grammar: a template keeps parameter names only, skipping the one word Object (form/form-stdlib/grammars/bml.fk:1425-1427, 4096), and instantiation compares the count of parameters and arguments and nothing else (bml.fk:4155-4160). The 2000 half is as stated.
why: The support list glosses the row as 'which kinds a template may wrap (757)' (grammars/bml-native-north-star.form:32-33), and bml-template-valid-kind? tests for a class or an interface (bml.fk:541-543). The hub 3.12.3 carries the same reading ('listed unsupported in 2026').
limit: The 2000 half was read at Java/jbml/Components/TemplateParameter.java:16, 21-29 and 33. That bounds were syntax only in 2000 is an inference by the node's own limit, under status observed.
by: r3/review-object-model-witness
at: 2026-11-24

