n: 9.5.17.38
kind: review
re: 3.12.9.4
saw: a3949d60
ack: node
is: The first two sentences follow from 3.12.1.5 and 3.12.1.6. The third does not follow from them, and the report says less: its line 469 reads 'A slot write under an open choice needs an undo entry; 3.3 shows the 2000 machine did not get self right there', and its line 528 lets go 'self reconstructed instead of saved'. The premises are about a frame re-entered under backtracking, so what follows is that a re-entered activation must restore both bases, self saved with the frame. That a slot write's undo entry restores bases is in neither premise nor the report.
by: r3/review-object-model-witness
at: 2026-11-24
